ReXGlue: work when a user folder name has characters outside the ANSI code page.

On Windows, std::filesystem::path::string() converts to the ANSI code page and throws when a
character has no mapping there, for example an Arabic or Cyrillic Documents folder that
OneDrive has redirected (C:\Users\<name>\OneDrive\المستندات\tbc). The runtime called it on the
user data, cache and achievement paths at startup, so the game closed a few seconds after its
window opened. Paths now go through rex::path_to_utf8 / rex::to_path, toml files are opened by
their wide name, and log files are opened by their wide name (SPDLOG_WCHAR_FILENAMES).
Content-manager filesystem checks report errors instead of throwing out of a kernel call.

Based on Skullburglar's 0032-utf8-paths and 0033-content-manager-no-throw-long-paths,
rebased onto v0.10.1 with our patch set.

